{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-job-25-1","title":"Job 25:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Bildad shews that man cannot be justified before God.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-25-2","title":"Job 25:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Dominion. 9:2-10; 26:5-14; 40:9-14; 1Ch 29:11,12; Ps 99:1-3; Jer 10:6,7 Da 4:34-37; Mt 6:13; 28:18; Eph 1:20,21; Jude 1:25; Re 6:16 he maketh. Isa 57:15,19; Mt 5:9; 2Co 5:18-21; Eph 2:16,17; Col 1:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-25-3","title":"Job 25:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>there. Ps 103:20,21; 148:2-4; Isa 40:26; Da 7:10; Mt 26:53; Re 5:11 upon whom. 38:12,13; Ge 1:3-5,14-16; Ps 19:4-6; Mt 5:45; Joh 1:4,9; Jas 1:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-25-4","title":"Job 25:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>How then. 4:17-19; 9:2; 15:14-16; Ps 130:3; 143:2; Ro 3:19,20; 5:1 how can. 14:3,4; Ps 51:5; Zec 13:1; Eph 2:3; 1Co 6:11; 1Jo 1:9; Re 1:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-25-5","title":"Job 25:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Isa 24:23; 60:19,20; 2Co 3:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-job-25-6","title":"Job 25:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JOB","chapterStart":25,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":25,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>How much less, etc.The original is degradingly expressive: \"How much less {enosh,} miserable man, who is a worm; and the son of Adam, who is {tol��h,} a maggot.\"</p>\n<p>4:19; Ge 18:27; Ps 22:6; Isa 41:14</p>"}]}